.\" Keep this page current: it describes the demo game demos/fruit3.bas (an executable made with BUILD, installed by "make install").
.TH ENGINE1999-FRUIT3 6 "November 2026" "Engine 1999 @VERSION@" "Engine1999 Manual"
.SH NAME
engine1999-fruit3 \- Fruit Invaders III, a Space Invaders style game with music
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B engine1999-fruit3
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fruit Invaders III is the third game of the series. New: the flying pineapple is a mothership made of three sprites (a sprite group) that flies by itself on a sprite path, and every fifth wave a boss arrives, a giant angry watermelon of 4 x 2 sprites (64 x 48 pixels) that patrols on a path, drops bombs and takes many hits (its health bar is at the top; a hit makes it flash white; 1000 points for beating it). Shooting stars cross the sky on paths of their own. Everything of Fruit Invaders II is still there. Fruit Invaders II is the rewrite of Fruit Invaders with shaded, animated sprites, a scrolling and twinkling starfield with a planet and a moon, music that gets faster with every wave, and more effects. Shoot the invading fruit before it lands: cherries are worth 50 points, strawberries 40, apples 30, oranges 20, lemons 10, the flying pineapple 50 to 300. Now and then a banana falls out of a fruit: catch it with the cannon for rapid fire (two bullets at a time). Bombs can be shot down. You have lives and get an extra life for every few thousand points.
.PP
The program is the demo \fIfruit3.bas\fR of Engine1999, made into an executable with
.B BUILD
(window kind: it needs the SDL2 library, nothing else); its BASIC libraries are inside it. It opens the Engine1999 window; the window can
be switched between the full screen and a window with F11 or ALT+RETURN.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.BR LEFT / RIGHT " or " A / D
move the cannon (only while the key is held).
.TP
.BR SPACE " or " UP
fire.
.TP
.B P
pause.
.TP
.B Q
quit.
.PP
A game controller works, too: D-pad or left stick moves, A or the right trigger fires, START pauses, BACK quits.
.SH FILES
The high score is kept in the file
.I fruit3.hi
in the folder
.IR ~/.local/share/fruit3/
(the driver
.BR local: ;
the file is safe there and needs no permission; a file of that name in the current directory, where older versions kept it, is still read when the new one does not exist yet; the game goes on without the file if it cannot be written).
.BR engine1999\-basic (7)
has the details, see FILES AND DEVICES.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine1999 (1),
.BR engine1999-basic (7),
.BR engine1999-fruit (6),
.BR engine1999-fruit2 (6)
